 ## Medium
 
-### [Pass 1] The visibility gate ignores two classes of content the function is explicitly able to render
+### Pass 1 — Blind Hunter
 
+#### Rules-bearing `pi` shapes can be rejected by the summary gate
+
 - **Severity:** Medium
-- **File:line:** `public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:246`
-- **Triggering input or sequence:** `updRulesSummary(pi)` receives a pool-info object whose only useful rules content is `rules_text`/`rules_source`, or whose only cost data is the structured `vitae_cost`/`willpower_cost` shape supported by `fmtCostLine(pi)`, while `effect`, `action`, `duration`, and legacy `cost` are all empty or absent.
-- **Observable consequence:** `hasRules` is falsy, so the entire Rules explanation box is hidden and cleared even though the function could render a full-rules expander or a structured cost. A qualifying power can therefore appear to have no explanation at all. The nearby comment explains why structured costs were excluded (to avoid Vampire Mechanics tiles), but it implements that exclusion by field shape rather than by pool category/type, so it also suppresses any ordinary power with that same sparse shape.
-- **Confidence:** High that the predicate has this behavior; medium, pending Pass 2 repository inspection, that such a sparse ordinary-power shape is reachable in current data.
+- **File:line:** `public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:261`
+- **Triggering input or sequence:** A caller loads a pool with `pi` containing only structured cost fields (`vitae_cost` / `willpower_cost`) and/or `rules_text`, but with no truthy `effect`, `action`, `duration`, or legacy `cost` value—for example, `loadPool(total, name, { vitae_cost: 1, rules_text: '...', rules_source: '...' })`.
+- **Observable consequence:** `hasRules` is false, so the entire Rules explanation box is hidden even though `fmtCostLine(pi)` and/or `renderRulesExpander(...)` could render meaningful rules content. The code comment explains why structured cost alone was excluded for Vampire Mechanics, but the gate is shape-based rather than category-based, so it also excludes any genuine power with the same sparse shape.
+- **Confidence:** Medium from the diff alone; repository call-site and `getPool()` tracing is deferred to Pass 2 as required.
 
 ## Low
 
-- None found.
+### Pass 1 — Blind Hunter
 
-## Pass 1 scope freeze
+#### The initial-hidden assertion also passes when the feature element is absent
 
-Pass 1 used only `specs/stories/code-review/rcv-3a-diff.txt`, as required. No repository source, story, tracking, or author-record file was opened before these findings were frozen. Within the supplied diff: every new DOM lookup is safely guarded (the box has an early return; body and cost are conditionally used), all rule-doc text entering new `innerHTML` is escaped or delegated to the stated escaping renderer, the `window` guard is additive in a browser, both new imports are used, the new CSS selectors are component-scoped, and no Playwright assertion was found whose success is trivially satisfied by zero matches or total feature absence.
+- **Severity:** Low
+- **File:line:** `tests/rcv-3a-rules-explanation-box.spec.js:176`
+- **Triggering input or sequence:** Delete or fail to mount `#rules-summary-box`, then run only the test named “the box is hidden before any pool is loaded.”
+- **Observable consequence:** Playwright's `toBeHidden()` accepts a nonexistent locator as hidden, so this assertion does not independently prove that the static disclosure was mounted. Other tests in the same file cover existence indirectly/directly, limiting this to a diagnostic-quality gap rather than a product defect.
+- **Confidence:** High.
 

