+# Adversarial review findings — rcv.3a
+
+## High
+
+### Pass 1 — Blind Hunter
+
+- None found in Pass 1.
+
+## Medium
+
+### Pass 1 — Blind Hunter
+
+#### Rules-bearing `pi` shapes can be rejected by the summary gate
+
+- **Severity:** Medium
+- **File:line:** `public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:261`
+- **Triggering input or sequence:** A caller loads a pool with `pi` containing only structured cost fields (`vitae_cost` / `willpower_cost`) and/or `rules_text`, but with no truthy `effect`, `action`, `duration`, or legacy `cost` value—for example, `loadPool(total, name, { vitae_cost: 1, rules_text: '...', rules_source: '...' })`.
+- **Observable consequence:** `hasRules` is false, so the entire Rules explanation box is hidden even though `fmtCostLine(pi)` and/or `renderRulesExpander(...)` could render meaningful rules content. The code comment explains why structured cost alone was excluded for Vampire Mechanics, but the gate is shape-based rather than category-based, so it also excludes any genuine power with the same sparse shape.
+- **Confidence:** Medium from the diff alone; repository call-site and `getPool()` tracing is deferred to Pass 2 as required.
+
+### Pass 2 — Edge Case Hunter
+
+#### Structured cost qualifiers are dropped before the reused formatter receives the pool info
+
+- **Severity:** Medium
+- **File:line:** `public/js/shared/pools.js:57` (missing `cost_note` in the returned rollable `pi`); observed at `public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:270`
+- **Triggering input or sequence:** A valid rollable rule has a structured numeric cost plus a qualifier, for example `cost: '1 V per effect'`, `vitae_cost: 1`, `willpower_cost: 0`, and `cost_note: 'per effect'`. `getPool(char, name)` builds the `pi`, then `loadPool()` passes it to `updRulesSummary()`.
+- **Observable consequence:** `getPool()` preserves the legacy `cost` and the two numeric fields but omits `cost_note`. Because `fmtCostLine()` gives structured fields precedence over legacy `cost`, the Rules explanation box displays `1 Vitae` rather than `1 Vitae (per effect)`. This removes mechanically significant cost information and can mislead a player about how often the cost applies. A direct Node reproduction against the real `getPool()` and `fmtCostLine()` returned `Cost: 1 Vitae` for the input above.
+- **Confidence:** High; reproduced with the real modules. The schema and cost parser explicitly support this exact numeric-plus-note shape.
+
+#### Repository-supported sparse rule shapes can reach the visibility false-negative
+
+- **Severity:** Medium
+- **File:line:** `public/js/shared/pools.js:57`; `public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:262`
+- **Triggering input or sequence:** A rollable discipline/devotion/rite/pact rule has a valid `pool` plus full `rules_text` and/or structured cost, but its optional `description`, `action`, `duration`, and legacy `cost` fields are absent, null, or empty. `renderCharPools()` calls `getPool()`, which passes `rules_text`, `rules_source`, `vitae_cost`, and `willpower_cost` through to `loadPool()`.
+- **Observable consequence:** Despite carrying displayable rules data, the resulting power tile loads with the box hidden because the four-field truthiness gate ignores every populated field. The repository schema requires only `key`, `name`, and `category`; the omitted summary fields are therefore a permitted stored shape rather than something `getPool()` rules out. A direct call to the real `updRulesSummary()` confirmed both rules-text-only and structured-cost-only inputs hide and clear the box.
+- **Confidence:** High for reachability through code and schema; current production-database prevalence was not established in this repository-only review.
+
+## Low
+
+### Pass 1 — Blind Hunter
+
+#### The initial-hidden assertion also passes when the feature element is absent
+
+- **Severity:** Low
+- **File:line:** `tests/rcv-3a-rules-explanation-box.spec.js:176`
+- **Triggering input or sequence:** Delete or fail to mount `#rules-summary-box`, then run only the test named “the box is hidden before any pool is loaded.”
+- **Observable consequence:** Playwright's `toBeHidden()` accepts a nonexistent locator as hidden, so this assertion does not independently prove that the static disclosure was mounted. Other tests in the same file cover existence indirectly/directly, limiting this to a diagnostic-quality gap rather than a product defect.
+- **Confidence:** High.
+
+### Pass 2 — Edge Case Hunter
+
+#### Malformed non-string rule fields render misleading coercion artifacts
+
+- **Severity:** Low
+- **File:line:** `public/js/suite/roll-v2.js:270-277`
+- **Triggering input or sequence:** A hand-edited or otherwise malformed rule reaches the roller with an object or array in `description`/`effect`, `action`, `duration`, or a cost field instead of the schema-declared scalar type.
+- **Observable consequence:** The code does not throw for ordinary JSON arrays/objects because `esc()` string-coerces them, but it silently paints values such as `[object Object]`, comma-joined arrays, or `[object Object]` as the visible cost. The Rules explanation becomes misleading instead of rejecting or omitting the malformed field. A direct call to the real function rendered cost and description as `[object Object]`.
+- **Confidence:** High for behavior; low likelihood under schema-valid writes, hence Low severity.
+
+## Pass 2 scope freeze
+
+Pass 2 inspected repository context but did not open the rcv.3a story or any author record. Every `loadPool()` call path was traced: rule-backed Discipline/Devotion/Rite/Pact tiles use `getPool()` and are the intended positive path; Skills, Custom Pool, Common Actions, Frenzy Resistance, Lash Out, Clash of Wills, Blood Bond Resistance, Humanity Check, combat quick-rolls, and direct test helpers all pass shapes that correctly leave the box hidden. `getPool()` normalizes empty summary strings to `null`, so empty and missing values behave the same in the gate and renderer. Replacing `rules-summary-body.innerHTML` destroys the prior expander button/body nodes, so the fixed expander id does not preserve an old `.open`/`.visible` state across power loads. `resetRollPool()` hides/clears the box synchronously before its general repaint. `sheet-helpers.js` has no other side-effecting top-level statements beyond imports and the guarded browser-global assignments; its imported dependencies inspected here also add no relevant browser mutation. No exact CSS class collision exists elsewhere under `public`, and the surrounding cascade introduces no override.

