+
+## Ship assessment
+
+**Needs patches before shipping; no blocking architectural problem.** The qualified-cost loss is player-visible and mechanically meaningful. The minimum patch is to preserve AC5's legacy-first behavior or thread `cost_note` through the existing `pi` path before using the structured-first formatter, with a regression fixture such as `1 V per effect`. The shape-based gate should also be made robust without admitting Vampire Mechanics—prefer an explicit power discriminator if/when the story permits the upstream shape change. The Low findings are hardening/test-quality issues.
+
+## Validation notes
+
+### Information barrier and files opened
+
+- **Pass 1:** Opened only `specs/stories/code-review/rcv-3a-diff.txt`. I did not inspect repository source, the story, or an author account before freezing the blind findings.
