/* Horizontal inset comes from #t-roll's own 20px padding, matching every
   other block in this tab (Again Rule, Rote/WP, Contested Roll, results,
   history) - deliberately NOT a left/right margin of its own. A prior
   version used `width: calc(100% - 32px); margin: 12px 16px 16px`, meant to
   self-inset by 16px each side - but with non-zero left/right margins
   present, the browser resolved the width as if the "- 32px" weren't there
   (measured: identical 845px box either way), so the 16px margins landed on
   top of an already-full-width box and pushed the whole button 16px right
   of every sibling below the Again Rule section. Zeroing the side margins
   is what actually fixed it - width alone or margin alone, tried in
   isolation, each still reproduced the misalignment. */
.rv2-roll-btn {
  position: sticky;
  bottom: 8px;
  z-index: 10;
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
